# Which browser checks a changed file needs: `pnpm prd browser --changed` reads
# this. AGENTS.md's Browser check budget table, as globs.
#
# One rule per line: a glob (bash pattern; * also matches /), then the checks it
# needs, or `-` for none, or `@suite` for every check. The first matching rule
# wins, so specific rules go above general ones.
#
# After the rules, two built-in fallbacks (browser.sh):
#   - a module under apps/web/app/lib/ (not lib/sync/) with a sibling .test.ts
#     needs no check: its unit tests cover it;
#   - any other file needs $unmapped_default (sign-in phase2 roundtrip), with a
#     warning to add a rule here.
#
# Add a rule when you add a screen, a check or a shared module.

# Docs, plans, tests and tooling: no browser checks.
*.md                                     -
plans/*                                  -
docs/*                                   -
.githooks/*                              -
scripts/loops/*                          -
scripts/backlog/*                        -
*.test.ts                                -
*.int.test.ts                            -
packages/*/test/*                        -
.nvmrc                                   -
.gitignore                               -
*.env.example                            -
eslint.config.*                          -
.prettier*                               -
vitest.config.*                          -
*/tsconfig*.json                         -
tsconfig*.json                           -

# The checks themselves. The harness runs the basics; a check runs itself.
scripts/browser-checks/cdp.mjs           sign-in roundtrip
scripts/browser-checks/proxy.mjs         first-sync layout-offline
scripts/browser-checks/*.png             -
scripts/browser-checks/*                 @self

